      "sample_index": 3,
      "text": "The common difference of the arithmetic progression is $(ab)-(a+1).$ So, $(ab)-(a+1)=b-(ab).$ Therefore, $b+1=2ab-a$, and  $b(a-1)=a-1.$ Also, $ab+(a+1)=b.$ Therefore, $a = b-a-1.$ Squaring both equations gives $a^2 + c^2 = 4ab + 2=a^2c^2.$ Therefore, $4ab-a^2c^2=2.$ But $4ab=0$ to achieve equality, so $a=0,$ which gives $b=0.$ Therefore, the answer is $\\boxed{2.}$\n1,001,001,010,001,001, = 18987 * 5455455 + 277 \n\n12037 * 1206501943 (this is small bit). Using 12000, 1000000, CD 2-digit format is no good. \n\nAlso, plain by interchange of last and penultimate bit, the RHS becomes instrumental. But observe that, if the third bit is odd then both the tens andVIOUS \nare odd and make fourth bit even. (if LHS is even, RHS is odd)\n\nSuddenly i wonder about notes of parity, squaring, shifting of digit thoughts! It reminds rs. from my class.  :rotfl:\n\nGoing through the suggestions on the wiki ...\n\nAnd not to forget \n\nhttp://www.artofproblemsolving.com/Forum/viewtopic.php?f=34",
